Chapter: CrfTruncatedTest
  cites Replay chapter ReplayCrf
  cites Replay chapter ReplayLog
  cites Net chapter MessageFraming
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A CRF is a replay log, so every length and the event count are whatever the
 producer wrote and the buffer may stop anywhere. Two separate defects are under
 test and they fail in different ways, which is why the fingerprints are read
 apart rather than together.

 THE CUT SWEEP is the truncation half. Every prefix of a whole CRF is decoded
 and its success recorded as one letter. A bound that is right by accident at
 one length shows up as a discontinuity; a depth that faults takes the run with
 it and prints nothing. `decode-schedule-event` indexed `list-at bs (off + 8)`
 raw, so a cut landing on a schedule event's reason byte faulted the guest
 rather than answering.

 THE COUNT ARM is the heap half. `crf-decode-events` was driven by the header's
 le32 with no relation to the buffer, so the count below -- 4294967295 events
 over a 27-byte log -- ran the loop four billion times pushing empty events.
 Measured 2026-08-16 with the refusal removed from the loop: `OUT OF MEMORY`,
 `SP=00000000bdfffbc8 HEAP=00000000b9e00010`, after 6 seconds. It kills the run
 rather than printing a wrong answer, so this arm cannot sit ablated beside the
 guarded one and the control was run as a source edit instead.

Section: Helpers

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "v" else "x"

  cut : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  cut (xs) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else cut xs n (i + 1) (acc & [list-at xs i])

 The count field sits directly after the two framed header texts, so its offset
 is derived from the encoding rather than hardcoded: 4 magic bytes, then each
 text as a 4-byte length plus its bytes.

  count-offset : Integer = 4 + 4 + 6 + 4 + 5

  poke : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  poke (xs) (at) (v) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs then acc
    else if i == at then poke xs at v (i + 1) (list-push acc v)
    else poke xs at v (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  set-count-ff : List Integer -> List Integer
  set-count-ff (bs) =
    let b0 = poke bs count-offset 255 0 []
    in let b1 = poke b0 (count-offset + 1) 255 0 []
    in let b2 = poke b1 (count-offset + 2) 255 0 []
    in poke b2 (count-offset + 3) 255 0 []

Section: Test Data

  event-session : ReplaySession =
    let s0 = session-new "myprog" "myctx"
    in let s1 = record-input s0 5 3 "recv" [10, 20, 30]
    in let s2 = record-schedule s1 2 7 SchedChanSendBlock
    in record-exit s2 1 0

  sweep : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  sweep (whole) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else sweep whole n (i + 1) (acc & yn ((crf-decode (cut whole i 0 [])).success))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let whole = crf-encode event-session
    in let empty = crf-encode (session-new "myprog" "myctx")
    in let huge = set-count-ff empty
    in let dr-whole = crf-decode whole
    in let dr-huge = crf-decode huge
    in act
      print-line-uni ("whole len=" & show (list-length whole) & " ok=" & yn (dr-whole.success) & " events=" & show ((dr-whole.session).event-count))
      print-line-uni ("count-offset=" & show count-offset & " empty-len=" & show (list-length empty))
      print-line-uni ("huge-count ok=" & yn (dr-huge.success) & " err=" & dr-huge.error & " events=" & show ((dr-huge.session).event-count))
      print-line-uni ("sweep 0.." & show (list-length whole) & " = " & sweep whole (list-length whole) 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("has off=" & yn (crf-has whole 9223372036854775807 8) & " n=" & yn (crf-has whole 0 9223372036854775807) & " sane=" & yn (crf-has whole 0 8))
    end
  end
